+
+### Keep hardware bridges inside Uke Control
+
+Do not add a runtime RPM for a userspace/kernel bridge. Integrate required session glue into uke-control, using separate internal layers or helpers in the same package when that reduces resource use. Healthy idle components must block on events; use demand activation and avoid periodic hardware polling or wake locks. Hardware protocols and lifecycle belong in kernel/DT, while compositor and session choices remain in userspace. Fold existing helper packages through verified ownership, dependency, configuration and rollback transitions before retiring their COPR producers.
